      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #78): complex ⌊ used to route its selected
      ⍝ operand through ComplexCell::zV(), which snaps a value within
      ⍝ ⎕CT-tolerance of an integer to an IntCell -- so a near-real
      ⍝ result that was not itself an integer got rounded to one, unlike
      ⍝ the real ⌊ path (FloatCell::bif_minimum_ff), which deliberately
      ⍝ returns the selected operand verbatim.
